eters-does-not-characterize-the-2003-marks-4-vbcbseya92ivpgf7.htm","timeAllotted":120000,"paperId":"aieee-2003","topic":"zeroth-and-first-law-of-thermodynamics","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["odd_one_out"],"yearKey":"aieee-2003","active":true},{"country":"in","examGroup":"jee","question_id":"Ftq3pX3kDVMovler","exam":"jee-main","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"subjectGroup":null,"subject":"physics","chapterGroup":"mechanics","languages":["en"],"chapter":"heat-and-thermodynamics","year":2003,"paperTitle":"AIEEE 2003","difficulty":"easy","topicName":null,"type":"mcq","examDate":null,"question":{"en":{"content":"The earth radiates in the infra-red region of the spectrum. The spectrum is correctly given by ","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Rayleigh Jeans law "},{"identifier":"B","content":"Planck's law of radiation "},{"identifier":"C","content":"Stefan's law of radiation"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Wien's law "}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"Wein's law correctly explanations the spectrum"}},"permalink":"the-earth-radiates-in-the-infra-red-region-of-the-spectrum-2003-marks-4-ftq3px3kdvmovler.htm","timeAllotted":120000,"paperId":"aieee-2003","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"topic":"heat-transfer","isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"aieee-2003","active":true},{"country":"in","examGroup":"jee","question_id":"DaO8lQ0ROBSNJEVc","exam":"jee-main","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"subjectGroup":null,"subject":"physics","chapterGroup":"mechanics","languages":["en"],"chapter":"heat-and-thermodynamics","year":2003,"paperTitle":"AIEEE 2003","difficulty":"easy","topicName":null,"type":"mcq","examDate":null,"question":{"en":{"content":"''Heat cannot by itself flow from a body at lower temperature to a body at higher temperature'' is a statement or consequence of :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"second law of thermodynamics"},{"identifier":"B","content":"conservation of momentum"},{"identifier":"C","content":"conservation of mass "},{"identifier":"D","content":"first law of thermodynamics "}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"The statement \"Heat cannot by itself flow from a body at lower temperature to a body at higher temperature\" is a statement or consequence of the second law of thermodynamics. This law essentially states that the total entropy of an isolated system can never decrease over time, and is constant if and only if all processes are reversible. In simpler terms, it implies that heat energy cannot spontaneously transfer from a colder body to a hotter one. \n<br/><br/>Therefore, the correct option is :\n\n<br/><br/>Option A : second law of thermodynamics."}},"permalink":"heat-cannot-by-itself-flow-from-a-body-at-lower-temperatur-2003-marks-4-dao8lq0robsnjevc.htm","timeAllotted":120000,"paperId":"aieee-2003","topic":"heat-engine-second-law-of-thermodynamics-and-carnot-engine","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"aieee-2003","active":true},{"country":"in","examGroup":"jee","question_id":"OC1Wl3iCwlWoYzF3","exam":"jee-main","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"subjectGroup":null,"subject":"physics","chapterGroup":"electricity","languages":["en"],"chapter":"current-electricity","year":2003,"paperTitle":"AIEEE 2003","difficulty":"medium","topicName":null,"type":"mcq","examDate":null,"question":{"en":{"content":"The nagative <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.993ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1323 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(723,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> pole of a Dani